MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Gameplay-neutral rendering optimizations for the bullet-hell engine
(collision/motion read JS state, never the DOM, so bullet count,
distribution, trajectories, and hit detection are unchanged):

- Element pools for bullets + orbs: reuse hidden div nodes instead of
  createElement/appendChild per spawn and .remove() per despawn, killing
  per-frame allocation/GC churn. Idle pool capped at 120; ACTIVE counts
  are never capped.
- Bullets/orbs positioned via --bx/--by / --ox/--oy CSS-var transforms
  instead of left/top, so per-frame updates are GPU-composited and skip
  layout reflow. Beam rotation rides --orot.
- Boss trail converted from per-frame unshift (O(n) memmove + fresh
  object) to an in-place ring buffer; per-ghost writes skipped when
  trail strength is 0.

No visual change at any tier; signature visuals (ground blur halo, 3
trail ghosts) untouched.
